#X obj 667 8 data.bimap;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 237 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 A bidirectional map container: stores pairs of left
and right keys \, and allows a fast lookup in both directions — by
left key to get the right value \, or by right key to get the left
value. Unlike [data.dict] \, which only maps keys to values in one
direction \, [data.bimap] guarantees that both directions are always
in sync.;
#X text 240 184 Typical use cases: mapping parameter names to controller
numbers (for example \, "cutoff" ↔ 74 \, "resonance" ↔ 71) \, translating
between note names and MIDI numbers ("C4" ↔ 60 \, "A4" ↔ 69) \, converting
between units with distinct labels ("kHz" ↔ 1000 \, "ms" ↔ 1) \, and
building routing tables where a name can be resolved in either direction.;
